<title>USA: Horizon Group Inc stake cut by investor.</title>
<headline>Horizon Group Inc stake cut by investor.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investor Alan Glen said Wednesday he lowered his stake in Horizon Group Inc to 800,495 common shares or 4.26 percent from 6.9 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, Glen said he sold 239,122 common shares between August 20 and January 14 at prices ranging from $19.1593 to $21.1250 per share.</p>
<p>Horizon, of Norton Shores, Mich., is a self-administered real estate investment trust that owns 35 outlet centers in the United States.</p>
</text>
